# Nougat OCR stub — QC-2208.04100

Status: NOT RUN.

Reason: this replication was a from-scratch qiskit + qiskit-aer independent reimplementation of the paper's Fig. 3(a) headline (bare vs RC power-law fits for iterative phase estimation under coherent noise). All numeric results were generated by executing our own code, not by extracting numbers from the paper PDF. Therefore Nougat OCR was not on the critical path.

Source paper: `work/paper.pdf` (arXiv:2208.04100v2, Gu/Ma/Forcellini/Liu, "Noise-resilient phase estimation with randomized compiling").
Plain-text fallback used: `work/paper.txt` (via `pdftotext`), sufficient for identifying claims C1–C5, the noise model in SI §IV, and the Fig. 3 fit exponents.

If a downstream consumer needs the paper as `.mmd`, run:

```
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --no-skipping
```

on a machine with the Nougat model cached (uicgpu / A100 preferred for the OCR skill's compute-target rules).
